          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మాట్లాడు (māṭlāḍu) is native Dravidian: māṭa, \"word\", and āḍu, \"to play, move\". DEDR 4834 lists māṭa and māṭal-āḍu, \"to speak\", with Kannada mātu, \"word\"; āḍu is DEDR 347."
