              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రాయి (rāyi) — \"write\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The everyday 'write'. Telugu and Kannada both kept the inherited Dravidian stem here rather than borrowing one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రాయి (rāyi) is native Dravidian. DEDR 5263 lists Telugu vrāyu and rāyu, \"to write\", with Tamil vari and Kannada bare, \"to write\". DEDR compares, with a query, Prakrit rajju, \"a writer\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That closes the run: look, listen, speak, write."
